 ut a production venue planning security beyond single projects.\n\nOrganis
 ation: Berlin Senate Department for Culture and Social Cohesion\nLocation:
  Berlin\, Germany. For professional groups (privately organised) and indiv
 idual artists in dance\, performing and performative arts without their ow
 n venue\, with their main working base in Berlin.\nAward: Two-year project
  funding (2028 and 2029) covering production-related personnel and materia
 l costs\, Berlin performance costs and certain general costs for developin
 g and securing working structures. No published minimum or maximum\; the a
 mount follows the financing plan you submit\, and only part of the running
  costs is co-financed. Fees in the plan should follow the Berlin minimum-f
 ee recommendations. No application fee.\nDuration: Calendar years 2028 and
  2029. Call published in December of the year before the deadline\; fundin
 g starts January 2028.\n\nMore: https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderun
 g/foerderprogramme/darstellende-kuenste-tanz/artikel.81996.php?utm_source=
 artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://www.berlin.de/sen/kultur/foerderung/foerderprogramme/darstellen
 de-kuenste-tanz/artikel.81996.php?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&ut
 m_medium=referral
